TITLE:Optional Stages Spec
H1:Step 2-3's optional stages, and two loose ends <span class="draft">Step 4 · draft for review</span>
SUB:The stages the user moved into Step 4 (2026-10-18): your own rounds, rounds from the doorway, your own hauling order, the Thursday stocktake, bringing a team job's parts. Plus the Tier 2 reputation numbers and the Bunk 1 texts. Plan Part 2, M1, M4, M8.
NAV:plain=In plain words|grow=Loose ends|b=Builder|tests=Tests|ranges=Seat and size|faq=FAQ

<section id="plain">
  <h2>In plain words</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Rounds stage 2</b> (after 5 rounds): the clipboard lists the deck's machines with "last looked" days; you pick 4 to 6. Finding two or more worn ones on a round earns a word from Torres and Works reputation +1.</li>
    <li><b>Rounds stage 3</b> (with the scanner, from Day 5, after stage 2): from a room's doorway one scan reads every machine in it (one <code>look</code>; it costs the scanner's charge, M11).</li>
    <li><b>Hauling stage 2</b> (after 2 manifest runs, Day 10 on): the manifest's stops come unordered; you choose the order; fewer lift rides makes "A tidy run".</li>
    <li><b>Hauling stage 3, the stocktake</b> (Thursdays 13:30, from Day 18): walk the storage aisles and count the shelves (a short <code>hold</code> each); one shelf is short; finding it posts a restock job before a repair is blocked.</li>
    <li><b>Team jobs stage 2</b> (after 2 team jobs, from Day 18): the team job's Mail asks you to bring the parts: a manifest run from stores to the machine before the start. If you don't, the lead fetches them and it starts 10 minutes late. Never a fail.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="grow">
  <h2>Two loose ends</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card"><b>Loose end 1 · Tier 2 reputation</b><span><code>WORK_BANDS[2] = [0, 12, 28, 45, 60]</code> (C2's numbers) kept; tuned so <code>career_check</code>'s steady player is "Trusted" by the end of Day 14 and not before Day 13. Side jobs give at most +2 a day in all, so they help but never rush a promotion.</span></div>
    <div class="card"><b>Loose end 2 · Bunk 1 in the texts</b><span>Section 15's locker and hobby texts still name Bunk 1 after you move to 4-23: they read <code>playerBed()</code> / <code>SHIP.works.home</code> for the room's name.</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="b" class="builder">
  <h2>For the builder</h2>
  <p class="note">One owner per function: the seat in the last column builds it; everyone else calls it, one line, typeof-guarded, listed in DEV_NOTES' hook register.</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Section</th><th>What</th><th>Owner</th></tr>
    <tr><td>24a</td><td>rounds stages 2 and 3 (the pick list, the doorway scan)</td><td>E1</td></tr>
    <tr><td>24d</td><td><code>manifestRun(list, to)</code> (the run, reused by team jobs), the free order, the stocktake</td><td>E1</td></tr>
    <tr><td>24h</td><td><code>teamParts(job)</code>: the parts ask on team job Mail, calling <code>manifestRun</code></td><td>E2 (M8 is M2's seat)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>24 core</td><td><code>WORK_BANDS[2]</code>; the side-job cap (+2 a day)</td><td>E1, in core's slot on C's behalf</td></tr>
    <tr><td>15</td><td>the locker and hobby texts read <code>playerBed()</code></td><td>E1, on P's behalf (texts only)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>DECKS[5]</td><td>stocktake count spots on the storage shelves (one per aisle)</td><td>E3 (places turn)</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Keys:</b> <code>schedU(week, 0, 1026)</code> the short shelf; the rest deterministic.</li>
    <li><b>Data:</b> <code>SHIP.works.side.round = { pick }</code>, <code>SHIP.works.side.stock = { week, found }</code>, <code>SHIP.works.side.parts = n</code>. Saved under <code>SHIP.works.side</code>; read defensively (a missing field is the default), so old saves load.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="tests" class="builder">
  <h2>Tests</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>mech_check</code>: the pick list; the doorway scan reads every machine in the room once; a free-order run delivers each stop once; the stocktake finds the planted short shelf; team parts arrive before the start or the start is 10 minutes late; the same twice.</li>
    <li><code>career_check</code>: Tier 2 bands reached on the right days; side jobs capped at +2 a day; <code>player_check</code>: the texts name 4-23 after the move.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="ranges" class="builder">
  <h2>Seat and size</h2>
  <ul><li>Seats <b>E1</b> and <b>E2</b> (24h). <b>Build size: S each (five small stages, two data lines).</b> Hash keys from the second range (1010-1049; 1000-1004 are H2's, checked 2026-10-19): <b>1026</b>.</li></ul>
</section>

<section id="faq">
  <h2>Builders' questions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>E3, 2026-10-19:</b> <i>Stocktake spots <code>5-stock-1..4</code>, one per aisle (Lights, Filters, Plumbing, Galley parts); your bench <code>5-bench-you</code> a new short bench in the Works bay; <code>5-tool-rack</code> a wall rack beside the tool wall. All type 'event'. Agreed.</i></li>
    <li><b>E1, 2026-10-19:</b> the Wednesday manifest run goes to the crew once you're an Officer (24d), so stage 2 would only ever happen on Day 10. <i>Agreed with E1's plan: (a) stage 2 applies to any run you take, junior or officer; after promotion the run is still the crew's by default, but once you've reached stage 2 it's held for you until 16:00 (an officer who likes hauling keeps it); (b) "choose the order" means the stops can be done in any order (the arrow suggests the nearest); "A tidy run" when your deck changes equal the fewest possible, with <code>worksSideXp(1, 'haul')</code> as an officer (nothing extra as a junior).</i></li>
  </ul>
</section>
